-- 146: SCENE B — A MINOR MELODIC. Built from ~/tunepile hooks, made to move.
-- Where 145 is an all-13 grid with a backbeat bolted on, this one is a straight
-- 4-beat dance frame (kick on the floor, snare on 2 and 4, offbeat hats) with the
-- melody as the whole point. Key: A MINOR, chosen so the hooks are used verbatim
-- rather than transposed — both of these are natively in A minor / C major.
--
-- Hooks (tabs-tidal via ~/tunepile):
--   * Melody (d6) — "Nothing Compares 2 U" (1990, Sinéad O'Connor / Prince):
--       g4 c5 d5 e5 d5 c5 a4 g4 — indexed from the tunepile tab:
--         "g4 c5 d5 e5 e5 d5 c5 d5 c5 a4 g4 ..."
--       Recut into a four-phrase 8-bar arc: statement, lift, descent, resolve.
--       Voice: mars_synths_DrSample_80s_Piano (n 0) — an 80s piano sample, played
--       in its natural register (c4-c5) per the rule below.
--   * Counter-line (d10) — "Losing My Religion" (1991, R.E.M.) mandolin riff:
--       d5 e5 d5 c5 f5 f5 f5 / g4 a4 b4 c5 a4 c5 — natively A minor.
--       Voice: `pluck` (17 plucked-string samples) for the mandolin feel, with a
--       3/16 delay throw.
-- Harmony: Am - F - C - G (bass d4 walks a1/f1/c2/g1 with a fifth on the offbeat;
--   pad d5 holds triads [a3,c4,e4] [f3,a3,c4] [c3,e3,g3] [g3,b3,d4]).
--
-- VOICE RULE (this is what bit us three times tonight): for a SAMPLE, `note` is
--   PLAYBACK SPEED, not pitch-from-a-sampler. A sampled voice must stay near its
--   natural register. Failures: gs3 on the marimba dragged it to molasses;
--   `|+ note 12` turned it into a squeak (2x speed); the OB_Strings pad voiced
--   down at b3/a3 (sample root ~C4) played at 0.6-0.7x and its tape wobble
--   stretched into a bassy "farting" chord. Hence: keep sample melodies in
--   c4-c5, use SYNTH voices (hoRhodes/orkRhodes) when real pitch is needed.
-- Mix: dry kit; space only on pad (verbSend 0.2) and the two melody voices (0.12).
--   Master aux returns are 0 (see sc/routing.scd) and the kit carries no sends.
setcps 0.5

d1 $ s "808bd*4" # gain 0.9 # shape 0.5 # hpf 46 # release 0.09 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d2 $ s "~ drumtraks:9 ~ drumtraks:9" # gain 0.75 # hpf 420 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d3 $ s "[~ drumtraks:4]*2" # gain 0.34 # hpf 1800 # lpf 11000 # pan 0.6 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d4 $ note "<[a1 ~ a1 ~ e2 ~ a1 ~] [f1 ~ f1 ~ c2 ~ f1 ~] [c2 ~ c2 ~ g2 ~ c2 ~] [g1 ~ g1 ~ d2 ~ g1 ~]>" # s "dubsynth" # waveMix 0.3 # cutoff 280 # fenv 1.4 # drive 0.5 # sustain 0.2 # release 0.2 # lpf 1300 # gain 0.7 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d5 $ slow 2 $ n "<[a3,c4,e4] [f3,a3,c4] [c3,e3,g3] [g3,b3,d4]>" # s "hoRhodes" # gain 0.62 # cutoff 2800 # release 1.2 # verbSend 0.2 # room 0.45 # size 0.5 # ddSend 0

d6 $ slow 2 $ note "<[g4 ~ c5 d5 ~ e5 ~ d5 c5 d5 ~ c5 a4 g4 ~ ~] [g4 ~ c5 d5 ~ e5 ~ d5 c5 d5 ~ e5 ~ d5 c5 ~ ~] [a4 ~ c5 d5 e5 ~ d5 c5 ~ a4 g4 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~] [g4 c5 d5 e5 d5 c5 a4 g4 ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~]>" # s "mars_synths_DrSample_80s_Piano" # n 0 # gain 0.72 # hpf 260 # lpf 8000 # verbSend 0.12 # room 0.35 # ddSend 0

d7 $ s "drumtraks:10(5,16)" # gain 0.3 # hpf 2000 # lpf 11000 # pan 0.45 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d8 $ silence

d9 $ silence

d10 $ slow 2 $ note "<[d5 ~ e5 d5 c5 ~ f5 f5 ~ f5 f5 ~ d5 d5 d5 ~] [g4 ~ g4 g4 a4 a4 b4 b4 c5 ~ a4 c5 c5 ~ ~ ~]>" # s "pluck" # n 0 # gain 0.6 # hpf 320 # lpf 7000 # verbSend 0.12 # ddSend 0.2 # lock 1 # delaytime (3/16) # delayfeedback 0.25

d11 $ silence

d12 $ silence

d13 $ silence

d14 $ silence

d15 $ silence

d16 $ silence
